msvcrt: mark a bare rethrow in the filter, not only in the __EXCEPT body.

`cxx_rethrow_filter` recognises a bare `throw;` (a CXX_EXCEPTION record whose object and
type parameters are both NULL) and returns EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER, but it leaves
`ctx->rethrow` alone — that flag is only set inside the corresponding __EXCEPT body in
call_catch_block4.

The __EXCEPT body runs *after* the unwind, and `cxx_catch_cleanup` (the __FINALLY for the
same catch) can run first. It then calls __CxxUnregisterExceptionObject() with in_use =
FALSE, which destroys the exception object even though the exception is about to be
rethrown. wine subsequently dispatches the next catch handler with a pointer to that
destroyed object; the handler reads a member the destructor has already cleared and
dereferences NULL.

Exception filters run before any unwinding, so setting the flag there is always early
enough. The __EXCEPT body still sets it, so this only tightens the ordering.

Observed in Baldur's Gate 3 (x86_64 guest under wine-arm64ec + FEX): a khonsu engine
exception thrown during level load is caught by an inner Anubis binding handler which
rethrows; the object is destroyed between the two handlers and the outer handler faults
reading offset 0x18 of the freed object. Verified by logging the exception object pointer
at throw, at destruction and in the catch funclet — all three were the same address, and
the destroy was recorded before the second dispatch. With this change the same session
loads a level, plays and round-trips a savegame with no faults.

Not arch-specific in principle: any x64 application that rethrows from a nested catch can
hit it. Not upstreamable due to WINE's AI contribution policy.
--- a/dlls/msvcrt/handler4.c
+++ b/dlls/msvcrt/handler4.c
@@ -380,7 +380,10 @@
     cxx_catch_ctx *ctx = c;

     if (rec->ExceptionCode == CXX_EXCEPTION && !rec->ExceptionInformation[1] && !rec->ExceptionInformation[2])
+    {
+        ctx->rethrow = TRUE;
         return EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER;
+    }

     FlsSetValue(fls_index, (void*)(DWORD_PTR)ctx->search_state);
     if (rec->ExceptionCode != CXX_EXCEPTION)
